<task id="CICD-071" project="ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Cutover (~4h window): restore Release matrix, flip branch protection to CI/Router only, enable merge queue (batch=1)</title>
    <status>complete</status>
    <estimated-effort>4 hours</estimated-effort>
    <phase>3 - Cutover</phase>
    <stream>A+B+C - Cutover</stream>
    <rigor-level>FULL</rigor-level>
    <autonomous>true</autonomous>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <dependencies>070</dependencies>
    <blocks>075</blocks>
    <tags>cutover, branch-protection, merge-queue, release-matrix, highest-stakes</tags>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    THE CUTOVER. Execute the ~4-hour synchronized window per spec.md §177-184 + design.md §177-191. Three settings flips: (1) restore `Release` to the `Build & Test` matrix in `sdap-ci.yml` (or its successor); (2) branch protection — ALREADY DONE 2026-08-29 via ruleset 21824191 (required check `Router`), so this flip is now a VERIFY step, not a change; (3) enable GitHub merge queue (batch=1, no speculative, queue timeout 30 min). Rollback playbook ready per spec §152 — pre-cutover snapshot from task 070 is the source.
  </prompt>

  <correction date="2026-08-29" source="session investigation; full detail in notes/branch-protection-enabled-2026-08-29.md">
    The original step 4 read:

      gh api -X PUT repos/spaarke-dev/spaarke/branches/master/protection \
        -F required_status_checks[contexts][]='CI / Router'

    That command had THREE independent defects and would have burned part of the 4-hour window:

    (1) THE ENDPOINT DOES NOT WORK ON THIS REPO. GET and PUT on /branches/master/protection both
        return 404 "Branch protection has been disabled on this repository" — with admin:true, a
        repo-scoped token, and a PUBLIC repo, so no private-plan limitation explains it. Rulesets
        are the working mechanism. CONSEQUENCE FOR TASK 070's SNAPSHOT: the 404 it recorded is NOT
        evidence that protection was deliberately switched off; the same 404 appears when the
        endpoint simply does not serve this repo. Do not treat "protection was disabled on purpose"
        as established.

    (2) THE CONTEXT NAME WAS WRONG. The real check-run name is `Router`, not `CI / Router`. A
        required context that never reports blocks EVERY PR permanently — the worst possible
        failure mode inside a cutover window.

    (3) THE PAYLOAD WAS INCOMPLETE. The classic PUT requires a full object: `strict` alongside
        `contexts`, plus top-level enforce_admins / required_pull_request_reviews / restrictions.
        A single -F field would 422 even if the endpoint were available.

    RESOLUTION: branch protection was enabled 2026-08-29 via ruleset 21824191 (PR required, 0
    approvals; required check `Router`; strict=false; force-push + deletion blocked) and verified —
    docs-only PRs still pass because `Router` is an always() aggregate that reports success when
    Tier 1 skips (#891, #892), and existing PR #887 went mergeable/CLEAN. Step 4 is therefore now a
    VERIFY step. What remains genuinely undone in this task is the MERGE QUEUE and the Release
    matrix restore.

    ROLLBACK: `gh api -X DELETE repos/spaarke-dev/spaarke/rulesets/21824191`. This supersedes the
    070 snapshot's rollback command (which targets the non-functional classic endpoint).

    strict=false is DELIBERATE and contradicts the 070 snapshot's stated forward target of
    strict=true. strict=true requires every PR branch to contain the newest master commit, so the
    first merge invalidates all other open PRs and each author must update and wait a full CI cycle
    — that serializes merging, which is exactly north star #2, and it reverses the 2026-06-05
    strict=false decision. The correct instrument for the semantic-conflict risk strict addresses is
    the merge queue (step 5 of this task).
  </correction>
  <correction date="2026-09-29" source="task-execute Step 9 verification against spec.md">
    STEP 2 AND ITS ACCEPTANCE CRITERION ARE WITHDRAWN. They instruct restoring the `Release` matrix
    to sdap-ci.yml during cutover. That directly violates a BINDING spec MUST NOT, and the successor
    workflow already names a different task as the owner:
      - spec.md:197  "MUST NOT restore `Release` matrix before Phase 2 deletion has merged AND
                      surviving suite green >= 7 days"
      - spec.md:128  FR-B07, same 7-consecutive-day rule
      - spec.md:225  explicitly records that this clock is NOT amended
      - ci-tier2-advisory.yml:249-250  "Debug-only is BINDING through Phase 2 per spec MUST 125 /
                      FR-B07. Restore Release here ONLY after surviving suite green >= 7 days
                      (CICD-075)."
    The 7-day soak IS task 075, which runs AFTER this task. Executing step 2 here would break the
    rule the soak exists to satisfy. Per project CLAUDE.md, spec.md is the binding source where it
    conflicts with a task file, so the spec wins.

    WHERE IT ACTUALLY BELONGS: task 075, in `.github/workflows/ci-tier2-advisory.yml` (the SUCCESSOR),
    NOT in sdap-ci.yml. The original step said "sdap-ci.yml (or its successor)" -- the successor is
    the operative half. Restoring Release into sdap-ci.yml would also have been self-defeating:
    task 077 DELETES that workflow ~14 days later, so the coverage would cost ~35 extra job-minutes
    per push for two weeks and then vanish, leaving zero Release coverage behind it.

    CONSEQUENCE FOR THIS TASK: step 2 and step 3 are SKIPPED, and acceptance criterion 1 is
    superseded by task 075's. This task's remaining scope is: verify branch protection (step 4,
    already done 2026-08-29), enable the merge queue (step 5), verify (6), test PR (7), monitor (8),
    record (9), merge #869 (9b).
  </correction>

  <correction date="2026-09-29" source="owner decision during task-execute step 5">
    STEP 5 (ENABLE MERGE QUEUE) IS DECLINED BY THE OWNER, and acceptance criteria 3 and 4 are
    withdrawn with it. This is a deliberate scope reduction, not an omission.

    MEASURED COST. A full CI run on a code change is 17-27 minutes wall-clock. At the specified
    batch=1 every PR runs CI IN the queue, serially, so the 17 non-draft PRs open at decision time
    would take roughly 5-7.5 hours to drain. That is the same serialization the owner rejected on
    2026-06-05 when choosing strict=false, and this task's OWN step-4 correction says of strict=true:
    "that serializes merging, which is exactly north star #2".  A merge queue at batch=1 is
    automated serialization rather than manual serialization -- better, but still serialization,
    and still against north star #2 ("CI must not hold up high-frequency master builds and pushes").

    MEASURED BENEFIT: NOT DEMONSTRATED ON THIS REPO. A merge queue guards the semantic conflict --
    two PRs that each pass alone and break together. The only such incident this project recorded,
    PR #934, was NOT that shape: #934 changed IOfficeService.QuickCreateAsync's signature without
    updating its caller WITHIN THE SAME PR. A merge queue would not have caught it. Widening Tier 1's
    compile scope to the whole solution (PR #944) did, and that has already shipped.

    So the queue would cost hours of throughput against a stated north star to guard a failure mode
    this repo has not exhibited, while the mode it DID exhibit is already covered.

    REVERSIBILITY is why this is cheap to decline: enabling a merge queue is a settings change that
    takes minutes. If a genuine semantic conflict lands later, turn it on then -- and prefer batch>1
    over batch=1 for throughput, accepting bisect-on-failure as the trade.

    CONSEQUENCE: this task's scope is now branch-protection VERIFY (step 4, done), pipeline
    verification (steps 6-7), the stability check (step 8), the record (step 9), and #869 (step 9b).
  </correction>

  <role>CI/CD engineer executing the synchronized cutover.</role>

  <goal>Branch protection requires only `Router` (already true since 2026-08-29 — verify); merge queue enabled; Release matrix restored; sdap-ci.yml still running in parallel (NOT yet deleted — that's task 077, gated by 14-day stability).</goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="pre-cutover-snapshot">projects/ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1/notes/branch-protection-pre-cutover.json (from 070)</file>
    <file purpose="spec">projects/ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1/spec.md (§152 rollback, §177-184 cutover)</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-C01">Merge queue: batch=1, no speculative, queue timeout 30 min.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec MUST">Keep sdap-ci.yml running in parallel through cutover+14d. DO NOT delete in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec rollback">Rollback authority is solo dev's judgment. Triggers: Tier 1 flake rate >2% sustained 24h; master green rate <90% over 24h; >3 false-positive blocks within 24h; merge queue stalls >2h with >4 PRs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project autonomous">FULL rigor; highest-stakes task in project. Step 9.5 mandatory.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Branch protection + merge queue flips</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1/notes/branch-protection-pre-cutover.json (rollback source)</file>
      <file>.github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml (Release matrix restoration target)</file>
      <file>.github/workflows/ci-router.yml (becomes the sole required check)</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Confirm 070 snapshot exists + is well-formed + meta document references the restore command</step>
    <step order="2">Restore Release matrix in `sdap-ci.yml` (uncomment lines 86-91 area; verify build runs both Debug and Release). Commit + push.</step>
    <step order="3">Wait for one full sdap-ci.yml run to confirm Release matrix builds green</step>
    <step order="4">ALREADY DONE 2026-08-29 — VERIFY ONLY, do not run the old command. Run `gh api repos/spaarke-dev/spaarke/rules/branches/master` and confirm ruleset 21824191 is active with required check `Router`, strict=false, PR required, force-push + deletion blocked. See the CORRECTION block below for why the previously-written command cannot work.</step>
    <step order="5">Enable merge queue: GitHub UI → Settings → Branches → master → Require merge queue (batch=1, no speculative, timeout 30min). OR via `gh api` if available.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify state: `gh api repos/spaarke-dev/spaarke/rules/branches/master` shows `required_status_checks` → `Router`; merge queue enabled. Do NOT use the classic `/branches/master/protection` endpoint — it 404s on this repo.</step>
    <step order="7">Test merge: create a trivial test PR; verify it goes through router → tier1 (blocking) → tier2 (advisory PR comment) → merge queue → merged</step>
    <step order="8">Monitor for the next 4 hours for any of the rollback triggers; if triggered, execute rollback (see spec §152) — restore branch-protection from 070 snapshot, disable merge queue, re-enable sdap-ci as required, document in `notes/cutover-attempts.md`</step>
    <step order="9">If stable through 4-hour window, commit cutover-success note to `notes/cutover-success.md`</step>
    <step order="9b">Merge PR #869 (dependabot: re-actors/alls-green 1.2.2 -> 1.3.0 in ci-router.yml). HELD until now on purpose: alls-green is the aggregation step in router-result, i.e. the job whose conclusion IS the `Router` required check, so bumping it mid-shadow-window could make prior verdict observations non-comparable. Its two siblings (#870 github-script, #872 cache) were verdict-neutral and merged 2026-08-30. Once cutover is done the window has served its purpose and this is free.</step>
    <step order="10">Step 9.5: code-review + adr-check on sdap-ci.yml Release restoration (other changes are settings, not code)</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="workflow">.github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml (Release matrix restored)</output>
    <output type="setting">Branch protection updated (gh CLI / UI)</output>
    <output type="setting">Merge queue enabled (UI)</output>
    <output type="notes">projects/ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1/notes/cutover-success.md OR cutover-attempts.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Release matrix restored in sdap-ci.yml; both Debug+Release build green</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`gh api repos/spaarke-dev/spaarke/rules/branches/master` lists `required_status_checks` with context `Router` (exact name; NOT `CI / Router`)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Merge queue enabled (batch=1, no speculative, 30min timeout)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A test PR successfully goes through router → tier1 → tier2 → merge queue → merge</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No rollback triggered within 4-hour window (or rollback executed cleanly if triggered)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">sdap-ci.yml still running in parallel (NOT yet deleted)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 9.5 pass</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes date="2026-09-29">
    COMPLETE. Record: notes/cutover-success.md.

    This task changed NO configuration, and that is the honest accounting:
      - branch protection -> `Router` was ALREADY DONE 2026-08-29 (ruleset 21824191); step 4 VERIFIED it
      - `Release` matrix restore: WITHDRAWN -- violates spec.md:197 / FR-B07 MUST NOT; owned by task 075,
        and belongs in ci-tier2-advisory.yml (the successor), since task 077 deletes sdap-ci.yml
      - merge queue: DECLINED by owner -- batch=1 serializes merging at 17-27 min/PR (~5-7.5h to drain
        17 open PRs) against north star #2, to guard a semantic-conflict mode this repo has not
        exhibited; the one real incident (#934) was intra-PR and is covered by #944's compile widening

    The cutover in substance happened 2026-08-29 and has run as the enforcing gate for a month.

    Stability (spec §152 rollback triggers), measured over 2026-08-30..09-29 rather than a 4-hour vigil:
      Tier 1 failure rate 0.0% (80 jobs, 0 failures) vs "over 2%" trigger
      master green rate  100.0% (60 runs, 0 failures) vs "under 90%" trigger
      false-positive blocks 0 vs "more than 3" trigger
      merge-queue stalls N/A (declined)

    Shadow window: SATISFIED (8/8, 0 false greens, 24.1/5 days) after PR #1028 fixed two script
    defects -- the readiness check could never fire once any false green existed, and the window start
    had not moved past #944's config change. Target 20 -> 8 recorded as an owner decision.

    Step 9b: PR #869 (alls-green 1.2.2 -> 1.3.0) was 754 commits stale with August CI; refreshed
    against master before merge. v1.3.0 is a SECURITY fix (GHSA-gj76-h2ch-5m76 template injection)
    with an unchanged input/output interface.

    sdap-ci.yml STILL RUNNING in parallel -- deletion is task 077, gated on the 075 soak.
  </notes>
</task>
